drafts={
1:{'en':['Your Cognition is traditionally described as Smell. You can explore whether the atmosphere of a place helps you notice distinctions before you can explain them. For example, compare two familiar working spaces and record the concrete differences in air, noise, light and distraction. A first impression can open a question; it cannot establish that a place or person is safe or unsafe.','When an impression matters, translate it into conditions that can be checked. Ask what changed, whether another setting gives the same impression and what information is still missing. Smell does not establish an ability to detect disease, dishonesty or hidden intentions. Use ordinary safety guidance and relevant expertise for those decisions.'],'zh-Hans':['你的 Cognition 在传统分类中称为嗅觉。你可以观察，一个地方的气息与整体氛围，是否会让你先注意到差异，再逐渐找到描述它的语言。例如，比较两个熟悉的工作空间，把空气、噪声、光线和分心因素分别记录下来。最初的印象可以提出问题，却不能证明某个地方或某个人安全与否。','如果一种感受会影响重要选择，可以进一步问：哪些条件发生了变化？换一个环境后，感觉是否相同？还有哪些资料没有取得？嗅觉分类不代表能够识别疾病、谎言或他人的隐秘动机。涉及安全与健康时，仍须采用实际证据及相应专业意见。']},
2:{'en':['Your Cognition is traditionally described as Taste. A useful way to explore this theme is through careful distinctions in direct experience: trying a small, reversible option, noticing what actually differs and deciding what deserves another attempt. Comparing two versions of a tool or a piece of work can make your preferences more specific than simply calling one good and the other bad.','Personal preference is not a universal measure of quality. Name the feature you value, compare it with the requirements of the task and allow other people to have different preferences. This reading does not prescribe food, a diet or a medical regimen, and it does not make a momentary liking sufficient evidence for a major commitment.'],'zh-Hans':['你的 Cognition 在传统分类中称为味觉。你可以从直接体验中的细微区别来探索这一主题：先尝试一个可逆的小选择，注意它与另一种选择具体有什么不同，再决定是否继续。例如，比较两种工具或两份作品时，把自己重视的细节说清楚，会比只说好或不好更有帮助。','个人偏好不是衡量品质的普遍标准。可以把喜欢的特点与任务要求分开，也容许别人有不同偏好。这一阅读不提供食物、饮食或医疗处方，更不把一时喜欢当成作出重大承诺的充分依据。']},
3:{'en':['Your Cognition is traditionally described as Outer Vision. You can explore how visible arrangements help you understand a situation: seeing a diagram, comparing examples or placing the relevant objects where their relationships can be examined. A shared sketch can also reveal that two people have been imagining different versions of the same problem.','What is easy to see is not necessarily the whole story. Compare the visible pattern with dates, definitions and information that is absent from the picture. Appearance alone cannot establish another person’s motives or predict an outcome. Use a visual reference to support inquiry, then revise it when the evidence changes.'],'zh-Hans':['你的 Cognition 在传统分类中称为外在视觉。你可以观察，可见的排列如何帮助自己理解一件事：看一张图、比较具体样例，或把有关对象放在能够看清关系的位置。一幅共同绘制的草图，也可能让参与者发现，大家原先想象的其实不是同一个问题。','容易看见的内容不一定就是全部事实。需要把画面中的模式与日期、定义及画面之外的资料比较。外表不能单独证明他人的动机，也不能预测结果。图示可以帮助提出问题，并应在证据变化时接受修正。']},
5:{'en':['Your Cognition is traditionally described as Feeling. This can be explored as attention to the overall felt quality of an experience: whether a pace, setting or interaction leaves you more settled, strained or distracted. Recording the circumstances alongside the feeling helps distinguish a recurring condition from a difficult moment.','A feeling deserves attention without becoming an unquestionable verdict. Compare sleep, workload, expectations and the practical demands of the situation. For important decisions, combine your chart’s Authority process with reliable information and appropriate advice. This classification does not diagnose a condition or establish that you can read another person’s emotions.'],'zh-Hans':['你的 Cognition 在传统分类中称为感觉。你可以从一段体验的整体感受来探索它：某种节奏、环境或互动，是否让自己更安定、紧绷或容易分心。把当时的条件与感受一起记录，能够帮助区别持续存在的因素与某一次困难的时刻。','感受值得被注意，但不必因此成为不可质疑的判断。可以同时比较睡眠、工作量、预期及现实任务要求。重要选择仍须结合内在权威的过程、可靠资料和适当意见。这一分类不诊断身体状况，也不证明能够直接读取别人的情绪。']},
6:{'en':['Your Cognition is traditionally described as Touch. You can explore whether handling a material, trying a device or physically rehearsing a task helps clarify what a description leaves uncertain. A short practical trial may reveal the grip, resistance or arrangement that matters for the actual work.','Direct contact has boundaries. Respect consent and safety, and do not assume that touching a person or object reveals hidden information. Describe what you actually noticed and compare it with other evidence. Where direct handling is unavailable or unsuitable, use an accessible alternative rather than treating the classification as a requirement.'],'zh-Hans':['你的 Cognition 在传统分类中称为触觉。你可以观察，亲手接触材料、试用工具，或实际演练一个步骤，是否能帮助自己理解说明文字没有说清楚的地方。一次简短试用，可能让握持、阻力或空间安排中真正影响工作的问题变得具体。','直接接触也有边界。须尊重他人的同意与安全，不把碰触人或物品当成取得隐藏信息的方式。可以描述实际注意到的内容，再与其他证据比较。如果不适合直接操作，应采用可及的替代方式，而不是把分类变成必须照做的要求。']}}
